{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Subgroup.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Center","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Subgroup.Center"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.classFn_factors_through_feedback","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.classFn_factors_through_feedback","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.lean#L92-L101","doc":"**Consequence for any conjugation-invariant reading.** A class function `f : H → R` (one\nthat cannot see conjugation) evaluated on a surface holonomy is determined by the boundary path\nholonomy *only through* the central factor: if `f` is also invariant under multiplication by\ncentral elements, then `f` is a function of `Φ h` alone. This is the precise sense in which a\n2-dimensional multiplicative integral carries no non-abelian content beyond its boundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.twist_boundary_eq_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.twist_boundary_eq_conj","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.lean#L86-L90","doc":"**The fundamental relation, one direction.** Writing `g := Φ h` for a surface holonomy `h`,\nthe twisting by the boundary holonomy is conjugation by the surface holonomy:\n`Ψ(g) = Ad_H(h)` (Yekutieli Thm 0.9.1, here immediate from Peiffer). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.exists_center_mul_of_feedback_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.exists_center_mul_of_feedback_eq","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.lean#L80-L84","doc":"The same statement with the central factor made explicit:\n`h' = z * h` for some central `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.eq_mul_center_of_feedback_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.eq_mul_center_of_feedback_eq","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.lean#L72-L78","doc":"**A surface holonomy is its boundary holonomy up to a central element.** If two elements of\n`H` have the same image under the feedback (as the 2-dim Stokes theorem forces for two\n2-holonomies over surfaces with the same boundary path), they differ by an element of `Z(H)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.ker_le_center","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.ker_le_center","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.lean#L59-L69","doc":"**The inertia subgroup is central.** In any crossed module, `ker Φ ≤ Z(H)`: for `k` with\n`Φ k = 1` the Peiffer identity reads `h' = k h' k⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule.peiffer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule.peiffer","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The Peiffer identity `Ψ(Φ h) = Ad_H(h)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule.equivariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule.equivariant","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.lean#L53-L53","doc":"`Φ` is `G`-equivariant for the conjugation action on `G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule.Ψ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule.Ψ","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The twisting `Ψ : G → Aut(H)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule.Φ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule.Φ","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The feedback `Φ : H → G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.CrossedModule","kind":"structure","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/CrossedModuleSurfaceHolonomy.lean#L44-L55","doc":"A crossed module `(G, H, Φ, Ψ)`: a group homomorphism `Φ : H → G` (the *feedback*), an action\n`Ψ` of `G` on `H` by automorphisms (the *twisting*), such that `Φ` is `G`-equivariant and the\nPeiffer identity `Ψ(Φ h) h' = h h' h⁻¹` holds. ","signatureChunk":0}]}